      "provenance": "literature_retrieved",
      "rationale": "Three independent ledger lines (L1, L2, L9) all name 'position Histidine 398 in the second extracellular loop' as the 2xHA insertion site; Python confirms res(398)='H' within ECL2 (396\u2013408). The phrase 'at position H398' is read as the tag inserted before H398 (insert_after_residue=397, residue_before=E, residue_after=H); insert_after_residue=398 is the \u00b11 alternative and both positions are fully within ECL2. L6 independently confirms that the ECL2 epitope tag in NT931 is predominantly labeled in intact cells, demonstrating efficient surface delivery. The N-terminal 3xFlag/YFP tags on the same NT931 construct (L5, L7) are intracellular and do not affect this extracellular site. Full-length NKCC1a and NKCC1b constructs bearing a 2xHA tag at position Histidine 398 in the second extracellular loop (ECL2, residues 396\u2013408) were expressed in primary hippocampal neurons (14 DIV). The same junction is independently confirmed by the NT931 construct (Addgene #49063, pcDNA3.1 Flag YFP hNKCC1 HA-ECL2) used in multiple studies. Surface HA labeling and confocal microscopy at 21 DIV confirmed plasma-membrane targeting.",
